{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607011816-ghosthacker-shiropico-standalone-repo"
  :title "ADR-2607011816: SHIRO & PICO (ghosthacker-shiropico) as a standalone west-managed repo"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "ghosthacker-shiropico-split"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-01"
  :authoritative_for
  ["SHIRO & PICO (the global-kids sibling series to Ren's Ghost Hacker, in the same GFTD cyber universe) lives at orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico, not nested under ai-gftd-mangaka/data/"
   "binary assets for this series (character refs, generated panels, motion comic) are NOT in this repo — they live in the separately-named DataLad dataset ~/gftdcojp/ghosthacker-shiropico-assets (B2 + IPFS), unaffected by this split"
   "manifest/west.yml registration for a single new project is done via the GitHub Contents API single-entry commit against origin/main tip, not a local edit + full bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb regen, when the local checkout's other child-repo pins have drifted from concurrent fleet activity (regen would bundle unrelated pin advances)"
   "git fetch showing '(forced update)' on a shallow superproject clone is not itself evidence of a real force-push -- verify with gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/compare/<old>...<new> before treating it as one (ahead_by>0, behind_by:0, merge_base_commit==old tip => false positive from shallow re-grafting)"
   "CORRECTION (same day): orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka, not ai-gftd-mangaka, is the structurally-correct production engine for this series -- SHIRO & PICO is an anime (work/episode/scene/cut, VOICEVOX, OP/ED, motion comic) matching animeka's cut-based 12-stage pipeline, and animeka's own test fixture already uses \"Shiro Pico\"/work-shiro as its canonical example. pipeline-specs.json's mangaka storyboardFromPrompt framing is a legacy/secondary path pending reconciliation. See :correction below."]
  :related
  ["CLAUDE.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2606282100-mangaka-render-commons-vs-sip-work-split.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607011500-ghosthacker-sip-atproto-actor.md"
   "manifest/repos.edn"
   "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka/CLAUDE.md"
   "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka/clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc"
   "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico#1 (docs/animeka-consumer-note)"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "user request 2026-07-01: 'shiropico は ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico でまとめて' (consolidate shiropico data into its own ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico project), during a session investigating Ghost Hacker manga progress"
  :investigated
  ["ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker-shiropico/ (SERIES-BIBLE.md, episode-01.md, character-design-spec.json, henshin-bank.json, pipeline-specs.json, ASSETS-DATALAD.md, episode-{11,12}-shotlist-v2.*.edn x10 langs) held a sibling series to Ren's Ghost Hacker, independently conceived (session be34e38d, 2026-06-18), targeting a different market/format (global kids anime shorts vs seinen manga)"
   "git ls-files revealed an episodes/ subdirectory not mentioned in SERIES-BIBLE.md's own file-manifest table: all 12 episodes scripted, plus ar/en/es/hi translations -- the series is materially more complete than its own docs claimed"
   "no code in ai-gftd-mangaka/clj/{src,test} referenced ghosthacker-shiropico paths (grep -rln returned empty outside the data dir itself), so extraction was safe with no dangling references"
   "ai-gftd-mangaka itself had just been split from ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/60-apps/ai-gftd-project-mangaka the same day via plain-copy + single commit + README.md.edn provenance note -- an immediate, reusable precedent"
   "binary assets were already routed to a separate, independently-named DataLad dataset (~/gftdcojp/ghosthacker-shiropico-assets) per the corpus's own ASSETS-DATALAD.md, so the text/data split had no binary-asset entanglement to resolve"]
  :risk "superproject manifest registration hit two live hazards this session: (1) git fetch showed '(forced update)' on origin/main repeatedly, which could mask a real force-push if not verified; (2) the local superproject checkout's main tip moved between commands (a concurrent fleet agent committing to the same shared working tree), and separately its other ~90 child-repo pins had drifted from their west.yml-committed values (unrelated fleet activity) -- a naive local edit + bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb + commit would have risked losing/misreading history from (1) and bundling ~90 unrelated pin advances from (2)"}

 :decision
 {:new_repo {:path "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico"
             :remote "gftdcojp"
             :visibility :private
             :method "plain copy of 85 git-tracked files from ai-gftd-mangaka/data/ghosthacker-shiropico/ -> repo root, git init, one commit, gh repo create --source=. --push (same pattern as the ai-gftd-mangaka split itself, README.md.edn records :source + :note instead of preserving history)"
             :head_sha "09cbea7ff5107e41387577a1450213d0c1c734f6"}
  :source_repo_change {:repo "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka"
                        :action "git rm -r data/ghosthacker-shiropico, commit, push to gftdcojp/main"
                        :unaffected "data/ghosthacker/ (Ren line) and all clj/ pipeline code -- zero references to ghosthacker-shiropico existed outside the deleted subtree"}
  :manifest_registration
  {:repos_edn "added \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico\" to :extra-projects, via GitHub Contents API single-entry commit (blob-sha-matched PUT against origin/main tip), not a local edit"
   :west_yml "added one project entry (name/remote/revision/path/groups, alphabetically after ai-gftd-gameka) via the same API method, mirroring the ai-gftd-mangaka entry's shape"
   :why_api_not_local "local git fetch/merge on the superproject was unreliable this session: (a) shallow-clone false-positive '(forced update)' warnings, confirmed harmless via gh api compare each time; (b) a concurrent fleet agent was actively committing to the same shared local checkout, moving main's tip between commands -- editing via the Contents API against the current server-side tip avoids both a stale-base 3-way merge and a race with the concurrent writer"
   :verify "pin == child repo HEAD confirmed (09cbea7... matches gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico@main); post-hoc re-fetch of both files via the Contents API confirmed the entries landed; `west update ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico` resolved and checked out the pinned revision cleanly"
   :deliberately_not_done "`bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb` was run locally to preview but its output was discarded (git checkout -- manifest/west.yml) rather than committed: the local checkout's other ~90 child-repo HEADs had drifted from what's committed in west.yml (unrelated concurrent fleet work), so a full regen+commit would have force-advanced ~90 unrelated pins alongside this one-line registration -- exactly the 'pin regression trap' repos.edn's :manifest-workflow warns about"}}

 :consequences
 {:decoupling "SHIRO & PICO's writing/i18n lifecycle (episode additions, new-language shotlists) no longer shares a repo, issue tracker, or commit history with ai-gftd-mangaka's render-engine/ComfyUI-fleet/D1-R2-Worker infra churn"
  :symmetry "Ren's Ghost Hacker line and SHIRO & PICO now both have standalone content repos (orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker and orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico respectively), rather than one having a dedicated repo and the other living inside an engine repo's data/ dir"
  :future_actor_target "a future self-sovereign atproto publish actor for this series (com-etzhayyim-tsumugu-style, per ADR-2607011500) has one independent repo to point at"
  :deferred_pin_debt "the superproject's other ~90 drifted child-repo pins remain unadvanced in west.yml after this ADR -- explicitly out of scope here, left to whatever workflow normally owns bulk pin advancement"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "leave ghosthacker-shiropico nested under ai-gftd-mangaka/data/"
   :rejected_because "couples an independently-written narrative IP's lifecycle to an unrelated render-engine/infra repo's churn; inconsistent with the standalone treatment Ren's line already has via orgs/com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker"}
  {:option "history-preserving git subtree split / git-filter-repo instead of a plain copy"
   :rejected_because "breaks consistency with the precedent this split follows (ai-gftd-mangaka's own same-day split from ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp was a plain copy + README.md.edn provenance note, not history-preserving); no concrete need surfaced for preserved blame history on this text corpus"}
  {:option "regenerate and commit manifest/west.yml in full this session (bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb with no --check)"
   :rejected_because "would have silently bundled ~90 unrelated child-repo pin advances (from concurrent fleet activity already reflected in the local checkout) into a one-line registration commit; used the GitHub API single-entry method instead, per repos.edn :manifest-workflow's stated canonical path"}]

 :correction
 {:date "2026-07-01"
  :what_was_wrong "original :problem/:decision framed ai-gftd-mangaka as the (accidental) parent repo and named no intended production engine; pipeline-specs.json in the moved corpus was in fact authored against ai-gftd-mangaka's storyboardFromPrompt (2D panel) convention"
  :correct_consumer {:repo "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-animeka"
                      :why ["own CLAUDE.md self-describes as \"mangaka（manga）の anime 版\" -- same team-based production-appview shape, atom is `cut` (shot, time-axis) not page/panel"
                            "domain model work -> episode -> scene -> cut (clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc) matches SHIRO & PICO's actual shape: 11-min episodes, VOICEVOX voice acting, OP/ED, motion comic (SERIES-BIBLE.md, episode-01.md) -- not manga pages/panels"
                            "12-stage pipeline (script/storyboard/layout/keyAnim/inbetween/colorDesign/finish/background/composite/edit/sound/delivery) is the anime production pipeline this series actually needs"
                            "animeka's own test fixture (clj/test/animeka/core_test.cljc) already uses {:title \"Shiro Pico\" :id \"work-shiro\"} as its canonical round-trip example -- independent prior evidence this series was already animeka's reference content, not mangaka's"]}
  :unchanged "the decision to split ghosthacker-shiropico into its own repo is still correct -- the content is engine-agnostic regardless of which engine consumes it"
  :followup "pipeline-specs.json's mangaka-shaped spec is legacy/secondary pending reconciliation to animeka's cut-based model (not done in this pass)"
  :landed_via "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico PR #1 (docs/animeka-consumer-note), amending README.md.edn's :engine-note"}}
